-## Executive Summary
-
-The MCT portal presents a mature, dark-first design system with tokenized color/typography/spacing (via `@mct/ui`), deliberate WCAG AA contrast overrides in the Tailwind config, strong keyboard navigation in both portal sidebars, `lang="en"` + skip-link in the root layout, a PWA manifest, labeled forms, and a lightweight axe-core E2E gate on 4 key pages. The 301-page surface is almost entirely covered by meaningful titles (291/301 pages render a title via `metadata` or JSX `<title>`), and skeletons/error boundaries exist at every route group.
-
-The main gaps are consistency rather than absence: (1) the mobile drawer in `SidebarShell` has no Escape key, focus trap, or focus restore ΓÇö the one notable keyboard-a11y hole; (2) page titles are split between the canonical `metadata` export (291 pages) and legacy JSX `<title>` (5 auth pages), and 5 pages have no title at all (`test-accounts`, `upload/[token]` are real pages; 3 admin redirect stubs are acceptable); (3) feedback UX is fragmented ΓÇö 5 bespoke toast implementations and 4 native `alert()` calls, no shared component; (4) Storybook contains 0 web-app stories (7 in `@mct/ui` only) and Chromatic only watches `packages/ui`; (5) the a11y E2E gate ignores non-critical/serious violations and scans only 4 pages; (6) dark mode is not implemented (dark-only by design ΓÇö should be documented as a decision).
-
-Recommended next actions: add Esc/focus management to `SidebarShell`, migrate JSX `<title>` pages and add titles to `test-accounts` + `upload/[token]`, consolidate toasts into one shared component, seed a few high-traffic web app stories and widen the a11y scan.
