-### Finding ID: DATA-P0-001 - Anonymous SELECT/UPDATE/DELETE on RLS-disabled PII leads table
-
-- Severity: P0
-- Confidence: High
-- Area: Data access / Privacy / Retention
-- Evidence:
-  - `supabase/migrations/5302038_disable_rls_public_interactions.sql` ΓÇö `ALTER TABLE public.public_interactions DISABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;` (the only RLS-disabled table in the schema)
-  - `supabase/migrations/5302116_grant_table_privileges.sql` ΓÇö DO loop grants `select, insert, update, delete on table public.%I to anon` for **all** tables
-  - `supabase/migrations/5302117_public_interactions_retention.sql` ΓÇö table comment: "contains PII: name, email, phone, message"
-  - `supabase/migrations/5302033_public_interactions.sql` ΓÇö CREATE TABLE (name, email, phone, message columns)
-- What is happening: `public_interactions` (contact-form leads with raw PII) has RLS disabled, and the 5302116 grant sweep gives the `anon` role full DML. The anon key is a public credential embedded in any Supabase client; the project URL is discoverable from the marketing site.
-- Why it matters: Anonymous visitors can `SELECT` every contact-form submission (name, email, phone, message) ΓÇö a PII disclosure; can also `UPDATE`/`DELETE` rows ΓÇö destroying the marketing lead pipeline and compliance records.
-- User / business impact: Privacy breach (GDPR-class), loss of lead data, reputation damage.
-- Security / privacy / reliability impact: Unauthenticated data exfiltration and tampering of a PII store; the retention design (5302117 + worker) is defeated because any attacker can delete rows early or read them before purge.
-- Recommended fix: `ALTER TABLE public.public_interactions ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;` + `create policy anon_insert_only for insert to anon with check (true);` + `create policy service_role_full for all to service_role using (true) with check (true);` + `revoke select, update, delete on table public.public_interactions from anon;` ΓÇö or scope the 5302116 loop to exclude this table. Fix the original INSERT failure cause (the 5302037-era INSERT policies should have sufficed) instead of disabling RLS.
-- Suggested validation: as `anon`: `select count(*) from public_interactions` ΓåÆ 0 rows / error; `insert` ΓåÆ succeeds; `delete` ΓåÆ fails. As `authenticated` (non-member): same expectations.
-- Owner suggestion: Platform/backend lead.
-- Effort estimate: < 1 day including re-test of contact-form INIT/SUBMIT flow.
-- Dependencies: 5302117 worker retention unchanged.
-- Status: Open (new finding this run).
